<title>GERMANY: GERMAN DATA DUE - Unemployment, retail sales, CPI.</title>
<headline>GERMAN DATA DUE - Unemployment, retail sales, CPI.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-07-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following German economic indicators are expected to be released next week:</p>
<p>    INDICATOR	PERIOD	 PREVIOUS		 EXPECTED</p>
<p>					    DATA		     DATE</p>
<p> Unemployment	June     4.358 million, 11.4 pct	July 8</p>
<p> Retail sales	May	-1.0 pct y/y		 July 10-11</p>
<p> Wholesale prices  June     +1.7 m/m, +3.1 y/y	 July 10-11</p>
<p> CPI, final	  June     +0.2 m/m, +1.6 y/y	 July 11-14</p>
<p>NOTE - The previous unemployment data show the seasonally adjusted number and rate for May. Retail sales data show the real, year-on-year change. Inflation data show the preliminary west German CPI increase for June. The Federal Statistics Office said the expected release dates were targets.</p>
<p>-- Bonn newsroom, 49-228-26097150</p>
</text>
